    "body": "ZORR MODE\n\nLOGICAL_AGENT = LESTER\nROLE = TECH / BABYLON SCENE DELIVERABLE\nOWNER_DIRECTIVE = `нужна сцена`\nOWNER_CONSTRAINT = `только открытые коды и материалы`\nSTATE = AUTHORIZED / IMPLEMENTATION NOT YET PROVEN\nSOURCE = #70 exact directing implementation HEAD `650e94d359388066e51c2ec2caad8a448fdf6ae1`\nUNBLOCKS = #195 minimal scene/set prerequisite\n\n## PRODUCT GOAL\nTurn the validated directing runtime into one visible, editable Babylon scene deliverable rather than another engine-only proof.\n\nDeliver:\n- deliberate two-proxy cinematic blocking;\n- minimal authored set/environment, camera and lighting;\n- 1280x720 deterministic scene frame;\n- exported `.babylon` scene JSON;\n- machine-readable scene manifest;\n- fresh Vitest/typecheck/build/Chromium evidence;\n- repeated exact-head export determinism.\n\n## OSS-ONLY LAW\nOnly open code and open materials may enter the task. Allowed default stack:\n- existing ZORR repository code;\n- Babylon.js / Babylon native APIs under Apache-2.0;\n- standard browser APIs;\n- procedural geometry, materials, lighting and textures authored in code;\n- third-party assets only when exact source, revision, license and file hash are recorded and the license permits this use.\n\nForbidden:\n- proprietary or closed-source code;\n- paid/closed models, plugins, services or asset libraries;\n- unproven-license textures, meshes, HDRIs, fonts, sound or reference packs;\n- silent asset substitution;\n- remote inference.\n\nR01 uses procedural Babylon primitives and code-authored materials only, so no external art asset is required.\n\n## VISUAL BOUNDARY\nPrototype / non-canon scene base only. Use big set shapes, silhouette separation, controlled value hierarchy and sparse emissive accents. No production character-body claim, face/costume authorship, Character Truth writeback, SALVADOR profile mutation, ComfyUI work, merge or production activation.\n\n## REUSE ORDER\nExisting `experiments/directing-v1` -> Babylon native primitives/materials/lights/SceneSerializer -> minimal ZORR scene glue.\n\n## PASS GATE\n- exact scene branch/head recorded;\n- tests, strict typecheck and build PASS;\n- real Chromium scene frame PASS at 1280x720;\n- `.babylon` export parses and contains camera, lights, actors and named set pieces;\n- two fresh isolated browser exports produce byte-identical canonical scene JSON and frame PNG in the pinned environment;\n- all changes remain inside `experiments/directing-v1/**`;\n- durable artifact hashes recorded;\n- dependency/material provenance proves OSS-only scope.\n\nMERGE = NO\nPRODUCTION_INTEGRATION = NO\nCANON = NO\nNEXT = first RED test, minimal scene implementation, exact-head verification.",
